<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44014" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖθριξ</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐΰθριξ</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐχος</span>, ὁ, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with beautiful
			hair</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eub.
				104
			</span></i> (lyr.); in <i><span class="en">
				Il.
			</span></i> always of horses, <i>with flowing mane</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἵππους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					23.13
				</span></i>
			,<i><span class="en">
				301
			</span></i>; of dogs, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyn.</u>
				4.6
			</span></i>; of birds, <i>well-plumed</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				18.57
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>fleecy, thick</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῆνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Al.</u>
					452
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>attached to a stout line</i>, of a fish-hook, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.52
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Carph.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
